WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Shinobu-chan's Special Napolitan</b>

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.480
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:35.680
<i>This is cabbage.</i>

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.110
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.650
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.620
<i>Yes, cabbage. Cabbage that hasn't 
even been turned to sauerkraut yet.</i>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:36.750
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:37.350
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.420
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.020
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.120
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:40.750
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:43.860
<b>Fizz</b>

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>Flavored with some sort of a salted 
seaweed and some other subtle seasoning.</i>

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.790
<i>That's all it's been seasoned 
with. Nothing else, and yet...</i>

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:51.760
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:52.930
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:53.530
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.800
<i>Why can't I stop?</i>

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.600
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:54.800
<b>Crunch</b>

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:55.470
<b>Empty</b>

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.410
<i>Oh God, that was a close one.</i>

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.870
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax Collector
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:04.300
<i>If it wasn't all gone, I might have spent 
the rest of my life eating cabbage.</i>

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.720
It's quite addictive, isn't it?

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.050
I'm sorry, but I cannot accept 
this as a valid dish.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.630
Even though it is indeed quite an 
imaginative taste, Fräulein.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.890
But by Aitheirian standards, 
full of history and tradition,

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:25.540
this dish strikes me as rather lazy.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.300
You think so?

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.670
If it tastes good, isn't that enough?

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:31.850
"Tastes good" being "enough"?

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.030
A woman of an uneducated people.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:40.510
That being said, I have yet to see the 
master of this store, that "Taishou-san."

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.770
He's out buying a few 
things we've run out of.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.950
I think it will take him a little longer.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.560
I could prepare you something 
simple while we wait.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.450
That's quite all right.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:55.350
I will have some more of this 
crunchy cabbage though.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.470
Certainly!

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.270
Hey, Hans.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.080
Are we really not going in?

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.770
I've been looking forward to this rare 
afternoon off where we can drink.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.180
I really don't want to deal 
with the person inside.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.940
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.940
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.490
You mean that cabbage gobbler?

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:11.690
Who is he?

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:15.020
That's the tax collector, Gernot.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:22.390
<b>Nobu</b>

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.670
Tax collector?

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.060
He's been hired by the city.
He goes around collecting taxes.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.380
You seem to know a lot about this.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.080
I saw him in my father's guild.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.230
He goes through everything 
the taxpayers have and then

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.380
forces them to pay a hefty amount of taxes.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.070
There are rumors that some 
of the tax collectors make

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.900
so much that they build themselves 
 really fancy palaces.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.530
So they're even worse
than the evil businessmen.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.590
The guild members were 
shaking in their boots.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.310
So what is he doing here?

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.210
Wait, you think he's got his 
eye on this restaurant next?

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.840
You don't think he's going to
put Nobu out of business, do you?

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.270
This is bad.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.200
Yeah.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:58.990
<b>Crunch</b>

00:02:58.920 --> 00:02:59.620
<b>Crunch</b>

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.160
<b>Crunch</b>

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:07.430
<i>This place suddenly opened 
its doors for business.</i>

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:13.100
<i>Since then, I hear it's gained immense 
popularity with the palace guards.</i>

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.910
<i>I'm sure they've made a 
tidy sum off of them.</i>

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.800
<i>If I play it right, I should 
make some good income here.</i>

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.090
<i>I just can't stop eating this.</i>

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.610
<b>Empty</b>

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.830
Another plate, sir?

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.490
Yes, however...

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.580
<i>This restaurant will be gone soon, too.</i>

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.040
<i>Before that happens, it might 
not be a bad idea to get a</i>

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.490
<i>sense of where its popularity came from.</i>

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.350
Is there anything you'd recommend?

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.930
I recommend everything here!

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.640
But Taishou's not here, so there are 
quite a few things I can't prepare.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.130
I see.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.380
<i>Harumph. Foreign letters.</i>

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.480
<i>Whatever.</i>

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.240
<i>The rumors say they serve Wurst 
and Kartoffel and raw fish.</i>

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:02.380
<i>Eating raw fish at some nameless restaurant 
isn't courage, it's straight-up foolishness!</i>

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.800
Hey, Fräulein! What is that?

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:13.050
Unless my eyes are playing tricks 
on me, that looks like pasta!

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.980
That's right, it's pasta.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.610
This is my lunch.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.010
I'll have that.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:21.060
Huh? But this is just for my own meal.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.700
Isn't eating pasta at an 
izakaya rather strange?

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.650
This is store selling food 
and I am a customer!

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:30.510
That is true, but...

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.150
I come from the south, originally.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:37.190
I ate a lot of pasta in my 
hometown when I was a child.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.230
It takes me back.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.090
I want some of that pasta, too.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:47.510
Okay. I'm fine with that, but I'll 
be picking the sauce myself.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.760
I can't fix anything complicated.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:53.340
That's fine. I leave it up to you.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:58.120
<i>That reminds me. I have yet to 
return home a single time since</i>

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.540
<i>beginning my career here as a tax collector.</i>

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.610
<i>Enjoying the flavors of my old 
home won't be a bad thing.</i>

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.080
Thank you for waiting!

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.520
<b>Shinobu-chan's Special Napolitan</b>

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.520
<b>Sweetness you can't get enough of!</b>

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.510
<i>Huh? It's red!</i>

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:12.380
<i>Outrageously red?!</i>

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.220
Fräulein, what would this be?

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.710
It's spaghetti.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.200
It's called "napolitan."

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.530
<i>I guess this is color is from tomatoes.</i>

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.570
<i>But it's so red!</i>

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.920
<i>Even down south where I grew up,</i>

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.940
<i>I've never seen pasta that 
was red all over like this.</i>

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:34.110
<i>Whether it's bolognese or puttanesca, 
pasta dishes usually have</i>

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.770
<i>a more reserved color scheme.</i>

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.720
<i>This is much redder than those!</i>

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.900
This seems to be made with 
peppers, onions, and bacon.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.220
Simple.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:44.820
Yup!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.220
That's napolitan!

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.440
This bacon seems high quality.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.490
You noticed.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.040
That thick-cut bacon is Taishou's favorite 
snack to go with his evening drink.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.550
It's rather good quality.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:01.300
I stole some, so even when he 
comes back, it's our secret.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.450
<i>You dug your own grave, Izakaya Nobu!</i>

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:06.690
<i>You may try to mask it with a humble setting,</i>

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:10.810
<i>but here's how I know you're 
squirreling your money away.</i>

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.670
<i>This thick-cut bacon is 
the unshakable proof.</i>

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:18.430
<i>That, and this glass you serve your ale in.</i>

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:22.540
<i>There's plenty of evidence 
all around this store.</i>

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:26.840
<i>Then there's no harm in me putting 
some of this proof into my stomach.</i>

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.960
<i>Tart... but sweet!</i>

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.140
<i>No, it's not just sweet.</i>

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:39.970
<i>This is literally the golden ratio of 
the tomato's sweetness and tartness!</i>

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:42.670
<i>Still, the flavor is childish.</i>

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.040
<i>Not something suitable for the 
palate of someone like me.</i>

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:48.520
<i>And yet, I can't stop.</i>

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.370
<i>What is this rich flavor 
spreading through my mouth?</i>

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:58.020
Sir, would you like some cheese and tabasco?

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.050
Cheese and tabasco?

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:02.060
It's a tasty addition.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.720
<i>Well then, let's start with this cheese.</i>

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:10.680
<i>This seems to be Käse, ground to a powder.</i>

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:15.660
<i>I would've never expected the tomato and the 
powdered Käse to suit each other so well!</i>

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:19.400
<i>Whoever thought of this pairing is a genius!</i>

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.750
<i>Next is this so-called tabasco.</i>

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:23.210
Oh!

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.170
It's spicy, so please only 
put on a little at a time.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.820
A few drops, just a few drops.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.450
<i>This...</i>

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.020
<i>Life... the universe...</i>

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.890
<i>The answer to everything!</i>

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:41.690
<i>The harmonious union of tart, sweet and 
spicy, spreading through your mouth!</i>

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:46.250
<i>On top of that mixture, the pepper adds 
bitterness, the onion adds mellowness,</i>

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:50.090
<i>and lastly, the thick-cut 
bacon adds gravity.</i>

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:54.840
<i>I'm experiencing God's love, 
"Agape", here on Earth!</i>

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.760
<i>What a meeting! What a joy!</i>

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:05.320
<i>And yet, this taste is so nostalgic.</i>

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.960
<i>It is not the taste of a faraway galaxy.</i>

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:13.610
<i>This taste, this taste 
overflowing with love.</i>

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.600
There, there.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.570
Don't rush! Slow down.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:24.870
I'm going to eat a lot and get big 
soon and grow up to be someone great!

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.850
I'm going to help people in trouble,

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.120
and pay back Mother and everyone 
else who has helped me!

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:31.230
I mean it!

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.360
Then eat up and we'll see.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:41.210
<i>I am ashamed of myself for saying this 
was childish when I started to eat.</i>

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:45.110
<i>This all-encompassing taste 
shows us the beauty of life</i>

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:47.900
<i>and the exalted nature of the cosmos.</i>

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:56.770
<i>Even this empty white plate is like a 
metaphor for the cruel, transient nature of life.</i>

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:02.600
You were eating with such gusto, sir.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.820
You must have been hungry.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:07.650
This is scripture in the form of spaghetti.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.930
Sir, is everything all right?

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.080
Yes, I'm fine.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.550
I don't need any change.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.310
But that's way too much!

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.190
I'll take my leave now.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.540
Weren't you going to wait for Taishou?

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.040
It's fine.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.450
A place like this, I won't be...

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.640
Sir?

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.930
It truly was a delicious pasta, Fräulein.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.960
That dish has allowed me to be reborn.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.060
Huh?

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:48.920
He just left?

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:50.970
What the...

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:52.110
What's going on?

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.210
Who knows.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.190
What's for lunch?

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.930
<i>I will quit this job that 
makes people hate me.</i>

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.730
<i>I'll donate the money I've made so far.</i>

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:06.710
<i>Then going back to my old home 
might not be a bad thing.</i>

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.050
Look at that man!

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:11.750
You shouldn't stare.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:15.750
<i>It seems that somehow these people 
walking down the street here</i>

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.760
<i>are rejoicing at my rebirth.</i>

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up is Nobu Plus!

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.430
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.320
Easy on the wallet and the calorie 
budget, these items are

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.780
perfect as a diet food or as a 
snack to have while drinking!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:47.440
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.440
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.640
Ryuu-chan, did you watch the anime?

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.540
I did.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.760
It was fun, huh?

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.070
Yes, at first I was really apprehensive 
about Gernot-san though.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:54.910
I know what you mean.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.130
But napolitan is just amazing, huh?

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.400
No matter who it is, it brings 
them back to being a child.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:08.720
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.620
I totally want a huge plate!

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:08.720
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.670
But I'm—

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:03.970
What, did your doctor veto that?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.840
How dare you?! I'm on a diet. A diet!

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.250
It's quite hard when you're my age.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.640
I see.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:08.900
Ey!

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:12.820
I have a secret napolitan that even someone 
who's on a diet can eat without guilt,

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:17.620
<b>Secret napolitan that even people 
on a diet can eat without guilt</b>

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:17.610
but still gives the impression 
of having eaten napolitan.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:22.600
<b>Bean Sprout Napolitan 
 [Ingredients (serves 2)] 
 Bean sprouts   300 g 
 Sausages   4  
 Onion   1/2 
 Peppers   2 
 Oil   as needed 
 Salt   a pinch 
 Sesame   a pinch 
 Water   3 tablespoons 
 Ketchup   3 tablespoons 
 Sugar   1/2 tablespoons 
 Worcestershire Sauce   1/2 tablespoons 
 Potato Starch   1/2 tablespoons 
 Powdered Cheese   to taste 
 Tabasco   to taste</b>

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:19.980
Oh, you use bean sprouts!

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:22.620
Those are low in calories, 
so that's perfect!

00:11:22.600 --> 00:13:05.730
<b>Bean Sprout
Napolitan</b>

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.750
Since the caloric value of pasta is a 
concern, we substitute bean sprouts for it.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.750
Other than that, the ingredients are 
exactly the same as regular napolitan.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:33.470
First, the onion; cut off the 
end, then slice it thinly.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:38.970
After you deseed the pepper, 
cut it thinly as well.

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:40.550
Right!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.630
What about the seasoning?

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:44.250
Right.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.060
What are you going to do?

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.580
Of course, using just 
ketchup is plenty tasty.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.540
But this time we're not using 
noodles, but bean sprouts.

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:49.810
Ah!

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.650
Bean sprouts are rather watery,

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:54.300
so if you give the sauce an extra 
punch, then it'll be even tastier.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:12:05.550
<b>Making the sauce -  Mix the following together:
Ketchup   3 tablespoons -  Sugar   1/2 tablespoons
Worcestershire Sauce   1/2 tablespoons -  Potato Starch   1/2 tablespoons</b>

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.370
You use the Worcestershire sauce 
to give the sauce some punch,

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.780
then you use the sugar for 
the sweetness and body,

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.870
and lastly, you use the 
starch to thicken it!

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.280
Not bad, mister.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:09.220
By adding the starch, 
the sauce gets tackier.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.850
Then it can really stick 
to the bean sprouts.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.630
Nice!

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.010
This is all so that it's as 
close to pasta as possible.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.640
I'm starting with the bean sprouts.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.110
Yes, let's go!

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:23.970
First, you stir-fry the bean sprouts 
to reduce their water content.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:25.320
<b>Lightly stir-fry the bean 
sprouts to get the water out</b>

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.330
I see!

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:27.890
This is done for now.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:29.180
Sausage.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:29.760
Right.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:31.590
Onion.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:32.630
Uh-huh.

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:36.650
From here, it's just like 
making regular napolitan.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:39.210
The peppers we sliced earlier.

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:42.180
The sausage is releasing
 its flavor already!

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:46.060
And then, lightly stir-fry this.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.600
Now the sauce we prepared earlier.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:47.910
Yes!

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:50.010
The starch sinks to the bottom,

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:52.260
<b>Mix the sauce well before adding it</b>

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.920
so always mix it well one
more time before adding it.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:54.370
Just toss it on.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.590
Mix it and toss it on.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:59.620
The scent of ketchup is
tickling my stomach!

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:01.560
The bean sprouts we took out earlier.

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:02.620
So this is when you add them!

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:04.610
Add the bean sprouts and mix it together.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:11.030
So, bean sprouts are a huge 
ally when you're on a diet.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:14.110
<b>Bean Sprout Napolitan</b>

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:14.130
They pair really well with ketchup, 
so they are amazing for napolitan.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:16.340
Please do try this dish!

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:33.000
<b>Today's High 
Speed Footage</b>

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:19.110
Yes, don't mind if I do!

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.650
This tastes just like napolitan!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.230
I could eat an unlimited amount of this!

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.480
My chopsticks don't want to rest!

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.410
But there's no worrying about 
the calories. Perfect!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.860
It's very easy. Everyone, 
you have to try this!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.040
It goes really well with rice as well!

